# The hardware service manager on the primary (V7R1M0), read only, as
# the service tools user QS_SST_ID names (sst-menus-primary.tn's). What
# IBM shows of a non-reporting resource and how one is removed: the HSM
# menu, its failed and non-reporting list and the logical resources menu.
# Menu selections and function keys only; no list option is typed,
# nothing is removed. 2026-11-07: QS_SST_USER lacks the privilege to
# start SST, QS_SST_USER_ALT signs on.
wait "Sign On"
signon
settle 3000
timeout 30000
key enter
settle 2000
type call qcmd
key enter
wait "Command Entry"
type STRSST
key enter
wait "Start Service Tools (STRSST) Sign On"
settle 1500
type {env:QS_SST_ID}
key fieldexit
type {env:QS_SST_PASS}
key enter
wait "System Service Tools (SST)"
settle 1500
choose "Start a service tool"
key enter
wait "Start a Service Tool"
settle 1500
snap sst-start-tool
choose "Hardware service manager"
key enter
wait "Hardware Service Manager"
settle 2000
snap hsm-menu
continue
# The HSM menu numbers its options "4.  TEXT", which `choose` does not
# read: the number is typed once the text is on the screen.
expect "4.  Failed and non-reporting hardware resources"
type 4
key enter
settle 8000
snap hsm-failed
show
key f12
wait "Hardware Service Manager"
settle 2000
expect "2.  Logical hardware resources"
type 2
key enter
settle 4000
snap hsm-logical
show
key f12
settle 3000
show
key f12
settle 3000
show
